+##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
+# Spec 040 scene of GiDet_CacheThreadExtremes (T116), not a visual test and without a reference image: occlusion() through a written irradiance
+# cache on a 16 x 16 image, which is one bucket (the default bucket size is 16 x 16). Rendered at -t:1, at the default thread count, at -t:2 and
+# at -t:16: with one bucket and 16 threads, 15 threads get no work. Colour, alpha, depth and the cache file must be byte-identical.
+# The sphere pair is examples/rib/tests/sphere-occlusion-reyes.rib's (the occluder needs `Attribute "visibility" "diffuse" [1]`).
+version 3.03
+Hider "reyes"
+Option "shaderformat" "default" ["rslo"]
+Display "gi-cache-thread-extremes.tif" "file" "rgba"
+Format 16 16 1
+PixelSamples 1 1
+Projection "perspective" "fov" 40
+Clipping 0.1 100
+Translate 0 0 5
+WorldBegin
+  Attribute "irradiance" "string handle" ["gi-cache-thread-extremes.icache"]
+  Attribute "irradiance" "string filemode" ["w"]
+  Attribute "irradiance" "float maxerror" [0.6]
+  Surface "occlusion_probe"
+  Sphere 1 -1 1 360
+  AttributeBegin
+    Attribute "visibility" "diffuse" [1]
+    Surface "matte"
+    Translate 1.2 0 -0.5
+    Sphere 0.9 -0.9 0.9 360
+  AttributeEnd
+WorldEnd
